---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { BRAND } from "../lib/brand";
---

<Layout
  title="About Us"
  description="Learn about Study Timer Online, our local-first browser study timer philosophy, and our mission to help students focus without distractions."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <section class="page-band" style="padding-block: 3rem 6rem;">
    <div class="container-page" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <article class="card legal-copy" style="padding: clamp(28px, 6vw, 56px); border-radius: 28px; line-height: 1.8;">
        <header style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.15); padding-bottom: 2rem;">
          <p class="eyebrow" style="color: #F59E0B; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">our mission</p>
          <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: #F8FAFC; margin: 0; line-height: 1.2;">About Study Timer Online</h1>
        </header>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2rem; color: #94A3B8; font-size: 1.05rem;">
          <section>
            <h2 style="color: #F8FAFC; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Building a Calmer Digital Sanctuary</h2>
            <p style="margin: 0;">In today's hyper-connected educational landscape, students are constantly bombarded by algorithmic notification loops, flashy advertisements, and bloated study platforms that demand tedious logins. We created <strong>Study Timer Online</strong> with a singular, unshakeable philosophy: focus tools should be serene, minimalist, and respect your attention. By merging modern architectural performance with a soothing <strong>study timer aesthetic</strong> visual mood, our platform gives self-learners, university scholars, and remote workers a dedicated cockpit for uninterrupted cognitive immersion.</p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 style="color: #F8FAFC; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">The Local-First Privacy Promise</h2>
            <p style="margin: 0;">Unlike conventional web applications that harvest personal study habits or force mandatory user profiles, our <strong>study timer</strong> is architected purely around local-first browser storage. When you plan daily tasks, configure Pomodoro sprint durations, or record focus streaks, all data resides exclusively within your own device browser. You retain absolute data sovereignty. There are no tracking pixels monitoring your study subjects, no hidden server databases, and zero barrier to entry.</p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 style="color: #F8FAFC; font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Engineered for Flow State Mastery</h2>
            <p style="margin: 0;">Whether you are implementing the classic 25-minute <strong>pomodoro study timer</strong> interval or simulating high-stakes timed exam conditions, our interface is crafted to fade into the background. Curated golden-hour typography, deep midnight gradients (`#05080F`), and crisp mint-teal accents (`#2DD4BF`) induce psychological calm. Every micro-interaction is optimized to reduce cognitive friction so you can focus 100% on learning.</p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
